iveness":0.9372091889381409,"text_excerpt":"I love Cafe 601. It's on the 11th floor of the Pan-American Life building and is open for breakfast and lunch on business days. I've never had anything bad here, but I can't say I'm too adventurous either. For breakfast, I normally get grits, eggs, and sausage; or a breakfast burrito; or a breakfast frittata with salsa. They have do have normal daily specials typical in NOLA (RB&R on Mondays, Fried/Baked chicken on Wednesdays, fried catfish and seafood gumbo on Fridays), but they also have burgers, other sandwiches (off the grill or from the deli), and a soup and salad bar every day. They also have a good assortment of fruits, snacks, desserts, and drinks. The prices are kinda medium. Not..."},{"business_id":"7nhfY3Z_d_0XD21m7Ha_dA","review_id":"XvWMe5eql-ffe0B-vVRpRg","date":"2012-04-02T18:55:14","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9109601974487305,"text_excerpt":"11th floor cafeteria in the Pan American Life Center. Another place I don't want to release the secret awesomeness of but I will because I care. Too many places around CBD charge you too much for a basic salad. But If all of you come here don't ruin it for me please. It's a good thing. They have a weekly menu and you can sign up for it to be emailed to your inbox. You can also see the menu on their website."},{"business_id":"7nhfY3Z_d_0XD21m7Ha_dA","review_id":"xkLe6oxEkzsLk3VK8Vfwbw","date":"2019-09-11T16:03:42","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.88679039478302,"text_excerpt":"Best kept secrete in downtown for a good affordable lunch. Glad I found this place on accident."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
